WEBVTT

00:04.020 --> 00:09.120
<i>When a person sees something extremely improbable,</i>

00:10.020 --> 00:14.340
<i>even before his brain can process any emotional response, he simply freezes... it seems.</i>

00:19.180 --> 00:21.120
Hiro-san, welcome back.

00:23.620 --> 00:24.800
Is something wrong?

00:25.040 --> 00:27.020
<i>Something wrong!?</i>

00:29.820 --> 00:31.620
I slept really well.

00:32.720 --> 00:34.260
Oh, 'Sup.

00:34.360 --> 00:36.140
Pardon the intrusion.

00:36.470 --> 00:39.180
Nowaki, sorry. Please get me a glass of water.

00:39.260 --> 00:40.560
Ah, Yes.

00:41.120 --> 00:42.580
Sorry Hiro-san.

00:43.060 --> 00:45.060
He's my senior from the hospital.

00:45.250 --> 00:50.780
We went for some drinks last night, and he missed the last train, so I put him up for the night.

00:51.030 --> 00:53.640
Senpai, here. Put some clothes on.

00:55.220 --> 00:56.570
Else you'll catch a cold.

00:56.860 --> 00:58.380
You too.

01:02.520 --> 01:06.400
Hiro-san, let me just tell this first,

01:06.820 --> 01:09.500
this isn't like "that"!

01:09.710 --> 01:11.260
Like "that"!?

01:11.750 --> 01:14.570
<i>Isn't it normally called just "that"?</i>

01:14.590 --> 01:16.220
Caught in an
illicit affair!!

01:14.590 --> 01:16.220
Actor Urasaki

01:14.590 --> 01:16.220
Scoop!!

01:15.070 --> 01:15.990
It's a scoop!

01:16.350 --> 01:20.870
Actor Urasaki, famously known to be happily married, was caught red-handed with another woman!

01:22.980 --> 01:27.980
A picture is worth a thousand words

01:28.310 --> 01:33.560
Afuredashita shoudou ga bokura no mune wo ustu

01:28.310 --> 01:33.560
An overflowing urge moves our hearts

01:31.740 --> 01:45.010
Junjou Romantica 2

01:33.560 --> 01:37.030
ima futari no story

01:33.560 --> 01:37.030
Now, our story...

01:38.320 --> 01:45.810
bokura no mirai ga kagayaite yuku yo

01:38.320 --> 01:45.810
Our future is going to shine on.

01:49.250 --> 01:54.540
mae ni susumeba dareka to butsukatte

01:49.250 --> 01:54.540
If I try to move forward, I collide with someone else,

01:55.010 --> 01:59.370
okubyou ni naru bakari

01:55.010 --> 01:59.370
and always lose my nerve.

01:59.370 --> 02:04.970
dakedo mae wo muite aruite iku yo

01:59.370 --> 02:04.970
But I'm going to face front and walk ahead,

02:04.970 --> 02:08.600
kimi to aeru nara

02:04.970 --> 02:08.600
if it means I can see you.

02:10.630 --> 02:15.610
ame ni utarete furueru koe

02:10.630 --> 02:15.610
Your trembling voice, pelted by the rain,

02:15.940 --> 02:21.210
nemurenu yoru wo samayottemo

02:15.940 --> 02:21.210
even if I have to wander sleepless nights,

02:21.890 --> 02:24.690
boku wa yuku yo

02:21.890 --> 02:24.690
I'll go,

02:24.690 --> 02:31.440
kimi to deaeru sono hima de

02:24.690 --> 02:31.440
Until the day when I can see you.

02:32.260 --> 02:37.450
Afuredashita shoudou ga bokura no mune wo ustu

02:32.260 --> 02:37.450
An overflowing urge moves our hearts

02:37.450 --> 02:41.160
ima futari no story

02:37.450 --> 02:41.160
Now, our story

02:41.320 --> 02:42.970
ugokidashita

02:41.320 --> 02:42.970
has started.

02:42.970 --> 02:47.960
meguriatta shougeki de iro no nai sekai ga

02:42.970 --> 02:47.960
The impact of our meeting, shocked this dull, grey world

02:47.960 --> 02:55.150
isshun de azayaka ni irozuite yuku yo

02:47.960 --> 02:55.150
and instantly burst into a brilliant color.

03:00.340 --> 03:04.910
<i>Professor Miyagi dragged me out and kept me up all night yesterday,</i>

03:05.610 --> 03:07.680
Woo! Come on, have another one, one more come on!

03:05.720 --> 03:08.980
<i>and I was dead-tired, body and soul.</i>

03:07.420 --> 03:09.010
I'm not drinking anymore!

03:09.190 --> 03:11.100
<i>But it was my turn to make breakfast today,</i>

03:11.100 --> 03:14.220
<i>so I went out of my way to hurry back here for Nowaki...</i>

03:15.030 --> 03:16.420
<i>and this is what awaits me?</i>

03:16.700 --> 03:17.810
Umm, Hiro-san.

03:18.860 --> 03:21.280
It'd be problematic if you misunderstood,

03:21.730 --> 03:23.570
but there really is nothing between us.

03:23.750 --> 03:25.510
He's your senior from the hospital, right?

03:25.610 --> 03:27.750
It's not like it's any of my business.

03:28.520 --> 03:29.540
Hiro-san...

03:30.000 --> 03:34.060
<i>Actually, when I'm not home, those two sleeping butt-naked besides each other,</i>

03:34.060 --> 03:36.980
<i>doesn't seem weird, isn't that thinking unreasonable itself?</i>

03:37.320 --> 03:38.800
Oh... Excuse me.

03:39.300 --> 03:41.360
I'll have two eggs please.

03:42.050 --> 03:44.730
Senpai, you said you had an early shift today, right?

03:44.820 --> 03:46.940
Hurry, get ready and go to the hospital!

03:47.200 --> 03:49.720
What's this? That's so cold...!

03:51.560 --> 03:53.430
Oh, I didn't introduce myself yet!

03:53.890 --> 03:56.520
Hello, I'm Tsumori, a pediatrician.

03:56.730 --> 03:59.680
Looks like you're taking care of Nowaki. Thank you.

04:00.370 --> 04:01.520
Same to you.

04:02.780 --> 04:05.350
Ehh... this is sort of a surprise.

04:05.760 --> 04:07.900
You're very different from how I'd imagined you to be.

04:08.080 --> 04:08.720
What!?

04:08.850 --> 04:12.090
This guy was saying how "adorable" you are,

04:12.150 --> 04:14.540
so I imagined a petite little girlfriend or something,

04:14.570 --> 04:17.220
but you're like the complete opposite...

04:17.870 --> 04:20.980
Oh, though I don't mind if it's a guy or a girl.

04:21.150 --> 04:22.240
It's alright.

04:22.570 --> 04:23.490
Senpai!

04:24.700 --> 04:29.270
Well, when he's outside the house, I assume full responsibility for taking care of him,

04:29.440 --> 04:31.060
so no need to worry.

04:36.980 --> 04:37.400
Yes?

04:38.090 --> 04:38.570
Eh?

04:39.800 --> 04:41.510
Yes, got it. I'll be right there.

04:43.450 --> 04:45.770
Nowaki, you're free today, right?

04:46.410 --> 04:47.520
Come with me to the hospital.

04:47.920 --> 04:50.190
They said emergency patients keep coming in and they're short on hands.

04:50.250 --> 04:51.830
Eh? No, but...

04:51.830 --> 04:53.700
Go. It's your job, right?

04:55.160 --> 04:56.070
Come on. Hurry!

04:56.460 --> 04:58.180
You can eat at the hospital.

05:00.000 --> 05:01.000
Sorry.

05:01.520 --> 05:04.160
When I get back, please let me explain everything.

05:04.370 --> 05:05.210
Nowaki!

05:05.600 --> 05:06.120
Yes.

05:13.350 --> 05:14.380
Excuse me!

05:15.620 --> 05:17.720
I forgot my watch on the table.

05:18.100 --> 05:20.110
Ah, there it is.

05:21.650 --> 05:23.530
Oh! That's right,

05:24.060 --> 05:29.740
Did you know that Nowaki's really torn about whether to become a pediatrician or stay in university, right now?

05:30.140 --> 05:32.150
He said he's thinking of moving sometime soon.

05:33.440 --> 05:35.500
Oh? You didn't know?

05:36.000 --> 05:38.320
I just assumed that he might have already told you.

05:38.540 --> 05:40.050
Sorry for saying something unnecessary.

05:40.880 --> 05:41.400
Bye.

05:44.640 --> 05:46.230
<i>What was that about?</i>

05:46.640 --> 05:49.540
<i>I never heard any of it before?</i>

05:51.430 --> 05:54.220
<i>Nowaki would never lie to me.</i>

05:54.580 --> 05:58.800
<i>That's why, even if I see him sleeping naked next to some other guy,</i>

05:58.800 --> 06:02.720
<i>"he's cheating" is something that would never cross my mind...</i>

06:03.280 --> 06:04.840
<i>...usually.</i>

06:06.680 --> 06:07.660
<i>But recently,</i>

06:08.080 --> 06:09.860
<i>things haven't been usual.</i>

06:10.720 --> 06:13.890
<i>Day by day, Nowaki's getting even busier,</i>

06:14.520 --> 06:17.820
<i>and as usual I've been immersed in my work.</i>

06:18.850 --> 06:25.210
<i>Even so, he's always clinging to me, saying "Hiro-san! Hiro-san!", until it feels really annoying.</i>

06:27.170 --> 06:30.950
<i>But lately, he seems to be pondering over something,</i>

06:31.400 --> 06:33.960
<i>and feels to be acting a little standoffish towards me.</i>

06:36.010 --> 06:36.940
<i>Anyway,</i>

06:37.390 --> 06:39.240
<i>it's different from usual.</i>

06:41.280 --> 06:43.340
<i>How many years have we been dating?</i>

06:44.840 --> 06:47.420
<i>Sure, if you're together with someone for a long time,</i>

06:47.500 --> 06:50.990
<i>the other person's presence might become just like air.</i>

06:51.460 --> 06:53.430
But...

06:53.580 --> 06:58.990
<i>So... about his career, it is because it's outside of my field that he didn't talk to me about it?</i>

06:59.690 --> 07:01.680
Then
what about moving?

07:01.970 --> 07:06.210
<i>The lease is upto next month, so he's taking this opportunity to move elsewhere?</i>

07:06.700 --> 07:08.200
With who?

07:08.360 --> 07:11.860
<i>I mean, I haven't heard anything...</i>

07:12.480 --> 07:13.630
<i>Does that mean...!</i>

07:14.960 --> 07:17.830
<i>In other words... he's...</i>

07:18.220 --> 07:20.200
Tired of me?

07:20.300 --> 07:22.560
<i>Wait, wait, wait! Don't rush!</i>

07:22.610 --> 07:24.620
<i>Think through this logically!</i>

07:24.710 --> 07:36.480
Nowaki is busy

07:26.070 --> 07:36.480
He started keeping
his distance from me

07:28.170 --> 07:36.480
Something is bothering him

07:30.440 --> 07:36.480
He doesn't say anything
about it to me

07:32.070 --> 07:36.480
He does say something
about it to his senpai

07:33.350 --> 07:36.480
They sleep together naked......

07:37.980 --> 07:39.980
He's tired of me?

07:44.400 --> 07:45.400
I'm home!

07:45.730 --> 07:47.010
Sorry, I'm late.

07:47.200 --> 07:48.820
Ah? Hiro-san...?

07:49.140 --> 07:50.980
Oh... Sorry.

07:51.170 --> 07:54.960
I was going through old books and somehow ended up filling the whole room with them.

07:56.240 --> 07:58.240
Just trying to relax and get my mind off things.

07:58.370 --> 08:02.500
Umm... this morning was all rush and bustle. I'm really sorry about that.

08:02.860 --> 08:04.750
Senpai said some rude things too.

08:05.660 --> 08:09.680
When I complained to him about it later, he said to tell you he's sorry.

08:09.890 --> 08:11.990
No, it's nothing much.

08:12.600 --> 08:16.100
Say, did you tell him that you were living with me?

08:17.000 --> 08:17.680
Yes.

08:18.740 --> 08:20.000
I... shouldn't have?

08:21.680 --> 08:23.040
Not that you shouldn't have...

08:23.610 --> 08:29.380
Listen, there are all sorts of people out there, so just be careful.

08:30.520 --> 08:31.310
Hiro-san...

08:32.660 --> 08:35.460
I... I haven't done it with senpai!

08:37.050 --> 08:40.080
Anyway, I don't care about it or anything!

08:40.080 --> 08:40.960
Hiro-san...

08:41.380 --> 08:43.700
So it's none of my business.

08:44.350 --> 08:45.100
Hiro-san...

08:45.150 --> 08:46.290
Shut up!

08:46.340 --> 08:52.300
Pediatrics, university, moving out- go do whatever you want, is what I'm saying!

08:54.630 --> 08:57.010
Why do you know about that?

08:58.170 --> 08:59.670
Did senpai tell you about it?

08:59.900 --> 09:02.100
Yeah, that's right.

09:03.240 --> 09:05.070
<i>What's with making that face?</i>

09:05.430 --> 09:08.020
<i>Did you really not want me to find about it that much?</i>

09:08.900 --> 09:11.840
<i>Somehow, I'm really angry.</i>

09:12.190 --> 09:13.780
Um, about that...

09:13.810 --> 09:16.040
I don't particularly mind though.

09:16.560 --> 09:20.080
Obviously, living closer to the hospital would be better, right?

09:20.260 --> 09:27.080
Actually, what makes me angry is that you didn't come talk to me about it first, is what I feel.

09:28.400 --> 09:33.700
Well, there might not be much point for you to talk to me about your career and technical stuff like that.

09:34.230 --> 09:36.660
<i>Oh! That's right...</i>

09:36.820 --> 09:38.050
<i>It's the usual, is it?</i>

09:38.120 --> 09:43.980
<i>At times like this, if I just reassure him with a gentle admonition, everything will go back to normal.</i>

09:44.560 --> 09:47.140
<i>If I say it, everything will be back to normal...</i>

09:48.140 --> 09:53.940
You're, once again, worried over catching up to me or surpassing me or some useless stuff like that, aren't you?

09:54.720 --> 09:56.240
They're not useless.

09:56.540 --> 09:59.180
For the you right now, it's obvious that it's impossible!

09:59.900 --> 10:02.580
And you've only been a doctor for one or two years too.

10:03.280 --> 10:04.900
Don't decide that for me.

10:05.200 --> 10:06.540
It's no use!

10:06.850 --> 10:08.960
I have my own way of thinking!

10:10.160 --> 10:12.580
I don't have to get caught in your words!

10:22.140 --> 10:23.190
Excuse me.

10:24.140 --> 10:27.020
I have to go help the doctor on duty. I'm leaving.

10:27.720 --> 10:29.140
I'll be back by morning.

10:38.230 --> 10:39.280
<i>Nowaki...</i>

10:40.070 --> 10:41.720
<i>...opposed me...</i>

10:55.740 --> 10:57.890
<i>I don't know what to do.</i>

10:59.580 --> 11:05.080
<i>I always took it for granted that Nowaki would always love me.</i>

11:05.810 --> 11:10.780
<i>For him, to go as far as saying something like that, he must have a very good reason.</i>

11:11.880 --> 11:15.450
<i>What should I say when he comes back?</i>

11:16.840 --> 11:18.260
<i>I'm scared to see him.</i>

11:19.880 --> 11:22.830
<i>What am I saying! I'm a 29 year old man!</i>

11:23.230 --> 11:25.170
<i>What happened to the demon Kamijo?</i>

11:25.250 --> 11:26.560
<i>What a wuss!</i>

11:27.880 --> 11:29.120
Ah, Kamijo, it's me.

11:29.820 --> 11:34.590
Sorry to call you on your day off. Could I get back the book I lent to you the other day, right now?

11:35.180 --> 11:36.480
I suddenly need it for something.

11:40.300 --> 11:41.580
Kamijo here.

11:41.970 --> 11:43.500
I brought the book-

11:47.900 --> 11:52.560
Ah! I-I-It's not like that! We weren't doing anything to be ashamed of!

11:57.600 --> 11:58.910
Kamijo!

11:59.440 --> 12:00.820
Please believe me!

12:00.820 --> 12:03.700
He just suddenly barged in here and somehow things ended up like this!

12:03.750 --> 12:05.320
No... so... that's!

12:05.320 --> 12:09.600
Not like I care about who you go out with but,

12:10.390 --> 12:13.600
that kid's still in high school, right? That's dangerous!

12:13.810 --> 12:16.080
Like I said, I didn't lay my hands on him!

12:16.160 --> 12:17.780
I mean, he's the dean's son!

12:17.880 --> 12:18.890
U-Uh...

12:19.000 --> 12:21.440
Yeah... I know! Don't even say the rest!

12:21.760 --> 12:26.900
Please, just don't do anything to ruin all of our work and achievements, okay?

12:27.260 --> 12:28.600
I know!

12:28.880 --> 12:32.590
Besides, this whole thing might just be a temporary whim of his.

12:34.460 --> 12:38.010
It's about time he started thinking seriously about his future.

12:39.020 --> 12:44.940
And if it looks like this old man's getting in the way of his future, I'm ready to end it any time.

12:48.620 --> 12:52.410
<i>I, too, don't want to get in Nowaki's way, ever.</i>

12:53.520 --> 12:58.680
<i>Letting every fleeting emotion control me will only ruin both of us. I understand that.</i>

12:59.100 --> 13:02.960
<i>And a relationship just running on its own inertia can only end badly.</i>

13:03.250 --> 13:04.350
<i>If that's so, better to just...</i>

13:06.660 --> 13:07.480
<i>Maybe...</i>

13:08.760 --> 13:10.700
<i>if I say that I didn't want to breakup,</i>

13:11.780 --> 13:14.340
<i>would Nowaki smile and say okay?</i>

13:24.400 --> 13:28.410
Kusama-sama, thank you for your business. I've found another property that matches what you were looking for the other day. I have faxed you the details for your reference. Please have a look.

13:35.690 --> 13:36.470
Yes.

13:36.970 --> 13:38.910
Ah, Hiro-san?

13:39.410 --> 13:43.800
Sorry, is there a bag, having a change of clothes, anywhere at home?

13:44.180 --> 13:46.300
The usual black Boston bag?

13:47.270 --> 13:49.130
It's here. On the sofa.

13:49.710 --> 13:50.920
Thank goodness.

13:51.600 --> 13:54.140
I was wondering where I forgot it.

13:55.060 --> 13:56.190
I'll come to get it.

13:56.430 --> 13:59.460
Oh, umm... should I bring it over?

13:59.800 --> 14:00.900
Uh, but...

14:01.420 --> 14:05.540
I'm free right now and it's on my way to the used bookstore anyway.

14:05.680 --> 14:07.160
That would really help.

14:07.590 --> 14:09.500
When you get there, please stop by the receptionist's desk.

14:09.720 --> 14:10.640
I'll come right away.

14:11.060 --> 14:11.940
Okay.

14:17.680 --> 14:19.680
<i>I felt a little nervous...</i>

14:21.040 --> 14:22.620
<i>What am I doing!?</i>

14:23.170 --> 14:24.600
<i>Pathetic.</i>

14:28.760 --> 14:30.320
Sensei, carry me!

14:30.350 --> 14:31.790
Me too! Me too!

14:32.420 --> 14:36.390
Hey now, he can't do everything at once. Sensei is very busy!

14:36.540 --> 14:37.820
It's alright.

14:38.040 --> 14:40.300
Okay! Everyone will get their turn!

14:44.320 --> 14:47.890
<i>He's the type of person who's naturally liked by everybody.</i>

14:48.800 --> 14:50.370
<i>The complete opposite of me.</i>

14:51.540 --> 14:54.340
<i>What do I want to do with Nowaki?</i>

14:55.520 --> 15:00.650
<i>One thing that is certain is, whatever Nowaki's "number one" is gets his top priority.</i>

15:01.050 --> 15:05.760
<i>And if I'm an unnecessary part of that, I should just part ways with good grace.</i>

15:06.680 --> 15:09.930
<i>If I do that, then neither of us will have to get hurt.</i>

15:15.180 --> 15:18.020
Ahhh! You're all so unfair!

15:18.290 --> 15:21.770
Kusama-sensei belongs to only me!

15:25.860 --> 15:29.110
<i>I must stop acting purely on emotion.</i>

15:29.110 --> 15:35.260
<i>Because, something like that's too uncool, unslightly and embarrassing...</i>

15:35.330 --> 15:38.360
<i>I could never ever do something so...</i>

15:38.660 --> 15:41.880
Don't you dare touch my Nowaki with your dirty hands!

15:46.700 --> 15:48.860
Umm, Hiro-san?

15:54.160 --> 15:56.480
Police! Call the police!!

15:59.160 --> 16:00.100
Hiro-san!!

16:02.540 --> 16:05.220
Sorry, my body just moved on its own.

16:05.220 --> 16:06.980
I'll turn myself in.

16:06.980 --> 16:07.820
No, umm...

16:07.820 --> 16:09.530
I'm no good.

16:09.630 --> 16:15.450
No, actually, senpai should recover completely in a day, since he got only a few scrapes.

16:15.590 --> 16:18.160
Forget it! I'm done for!

16:18.160 --> 16:20.500
I can't be calm and composed like I used to be!

16:20.560 --> 16:24.720
If I can't keep a handle on my own actions, I'm finished as an educator!

16:24.720 --> 16:26.280
Hiro-san, still...

16:26.330 --> 16:27.860
I mean, what is this!?

16:32.760 --> 16:34.340
This is a nice place.

16:35.640 --> 16:38.830
It's close to the university and the floor plan looks very easy to use.

16:40.480 --> 16:41.620
<i>As I thought!</i>

16:42.100 --> 16:42.870
Hiro-san.

16:43.060 --> 16:44.870
<i>Are you going to tell me to break up?</i>

16:45.120 --> 16:47.710
Would you like to move in with me?

16:52.820 --> 16:53.320
What?

16:53.790 --> 16:56.820
I'll take care of everything with the lease, so it's alright.

16:57.500 --> 16:59.960
I have all the necessary funds in savings.

17:00.120 --> 17:00.840
What!?

17:02.210 --> 17:03.190
Sorry.

17:03.770 --> 17:06.720
I wanted to tell you after all the details had been finalized.

17:07.040 --> 17:10.220
But senpai went ahead and said something unnecessary, messing up everything.

17:11.320 --> 17:15.130
Uh, you... aren't moving in with that senpai of yours?

17:15.180 --> 17:15.660
Eh?

17:16.390 --> 17:17.900
No, because...

17:18.340 --> 17:20.240
...you'd me breaking up with me...

17:20.890 --> 17:21.420
What?

17:22.080 --> 17:23.010
Who is?

17:24.000 --> 17:24.980
Why?

17:26.060 --> 17:28.430
That's what I want to know.

17:28.740 --> 17:29.620
Umm...

17:30.120 --> 17:33.890
I'm being obstinate but there's nothing between me and senpai.

17:35.540 --> 17:37.040
Let me explain.

17:37.040 --> 17:38.000
Shake

17:37.150 --> 17:39.290
Senpai, please sleep on the bed.

17:39.280 --> 17:40.130
Shake

17:39.290 --> 17:40.400
You'll catch a cold.

17:42.950 --> 17:44.060
Geez...!

17:44.770 --> 17:45.880
Let's turn on the floor heater.

17:47.870 --> 17:49.360
I wonder if it's warm enough.

17:55.080 --> 17:56.570
...and that's how it is.

17:58.500 --> 17:59.820
Please don't worry.

18:00.650 --> 18:03.340
I won't embrace anyone except you.

18:04.000 --> 18:06.260
A-A-Are you an idiot!?

18:06.260 --> 18:07.980
Besides, what the hell is this!?

18:08.040 --> 18:10.790
If you wanted to move out, why didn't you say anything about it?

18:10.920 --> 18:13.440
I wouldn't have minded just renewing our lease!

18:14.360 --> 18:17.840
There's no point if you're not living somewhere that <i>I</i> signed for.

18:18.110 --> 18:18.980
What!?

18:20.140 --> 18:23.320
You might have already forgotten it.

18:24.140 --> 18:28.040
Do you remember that one time we were talking over drinks?

18:29.980 --> 18:33.630
You were talking about a professor at university and Usami-san.

18:35.460 --> 18:41.930
Professor Miyagi and Akihiko, they both are completely hopeless cases,

18:42.140 --> 18:45.840
but when it comes to work, I just can't help but respect them.

18:45.840 --> 18:49.520
Once they set a goal, they carry it through to the end.

18:50.300 --> 18:53.640
Something like that, just saying it is simple.

18:54.020 --> 18:58.010
But there aren't many people who actually pull it off!

18:58.300 --> 19:01.560
People like that are the once I really feel like following,

19:01.720 --> 19:04.110
look up to them and follow their example.

19:04.740 --> 19:10.510
Whether they are men or women, people who live like daredevils, are the ones I like.

19:12.020 --> 19:14.960
I... said all that?

19:16.330 --> 19:18.580
Catching up or surpassing you,

19:18.930 --> 19:22.560
you said I didn't have to think about it all the time.

19:23.550 --> 19:25.450
I, too, thought it's okay.

19:26.450 --> 19:29.320
But I realized that it's no good.

19:29.620 --> 19:34.980
I immediately get jealous of anyone you like,

19:35.440 --> 19:41.340
and feeling jealous means those people posses something that I don't.

19:42.800 --> 19:50.390
My goal is to become a man who can protect and support you, both mentally and societally.

19:51.820 --> 19:56.920
That's why, like always, I can't be satisfied with letting myself be comforted by you.

19:58.020 --> 20:00.410
Thinking about financially helping you,

20:00.580 --> 20:03.050
staying in university seemed to be the best choice.

20:03.680 --> 20:07.790
But it's my dream to be involved in emergency medical care for children.

20:08.110 --> 20:11.140
Giving up on that seemed to be degrading from my liking.

20:11.740 --> 20:14.490
So instead, I started on things I could do right now.

20:15.920 --> 20:22.080
L-Let's see... ah! So, what, this is like, "Come to my house and be my bride!," right?

20:24.180 --> 20:24.960
Bride!?

20:25.580 --> 20:28.310
No, no, I mean, who's the bride here, right?

20:30.320 --> 20:33.070
You can consider all of this as my selfish request.

20:33.210 --> 20:36.200
But there's one thing that I wouldn't want you to forget,

20:36.200 --> 20:38.200
my world revolves around you, every single moment.

20:43.670 --> 20:45.820
Please absolutely never forget this.

20:47.100 --> 20:49.610
<i>While I was moping around little things, </i>

20:49.840 --> 20:53.500
<i>one step at a time, he was moving forward,</i>

20:54.240 --> 20:55.520
<i>for himself...</i>

20:56.910 --> 20:59.400
For me?

21:00.230 --> 21:02.260
I'm sorry, it's stupid.

21:02.680 --> 21:04.440
Don't call it stupid.

21:05.710 --> 21:06.920
I get it.

21:07.370 --> 21:09.180
Sheesh, it can't be helped.

21:10.620 --> 21:12.030
<i>I'm stupid.</i>

21:12.480 --> 21:13.850
<i>This is troubling.</i>

21:14.400 --> 21:15.700
<i>I'm happy.</i>

21:17.960 --> 21:20.400
<i>For real, I...</i>

21:22.650 --> 21:24.400
<i>...like him.</i>

21:26.220 --> 21:30.160
Are you an idiot!? What do you think you are doing!? What if people saw...!

21:30.160 --> 21:31.340
Yes, Hiro-san.

21:31.680 --> 21:35.090
So, when we get home, let's do it a lot, okay?

21:36.750 --> 21:38.060
<i>He really is an idiot.</i>

21:38.760 --> 21:42.010
<i>But, for loving an idiot like that, I too...</i>

21:54.020 --> 21:59.160
Crossing paths at the end of the day,

21:59.290 --> 22:04.550
itsu kara ka kimi ga sakimawari shite matte ite

21:59.290 --> 22:04.550
at some point you went up ahead and waited for me.

22:04.900 --> 22:09.920
ureshii kimochi bai ni shite kurete

22:04.900 --> 22:09.920
You doubled all my happiness,

22:09.920 --> 22:16.610
kanamishi kimochi hanbun ni shite kureru kara

22:09.920 --> 22:16.610
and halved all my sadness.

22:16.720 --> 22:21.720
kore kara donna michi aruitemo

22:16.720 --> 22:21.720
No matter what path I walk in the future,

22:22.120 --> 22:26.400
kitto sore wa kimi he to tsuzuiteru

22:22.120 --> 22:26.400
will surely lead to you.

22:26.400 --> 22:29.160
boku no saki ni wa kimi ga ite

22:26.400 --> 22:29.160
You're there up ahead of me,

22:29.160 --> 22:32.020
kimi no saki ni wa boka ga iru

22:29.160 --> 22:32.020
I'm there ahead of you,

22:32.020 --> 22:37.290
hoka no dare mo inai futari dake no basho

22:32.020 --> 22:37.290
A place for just the two of us with no one else around.

22:37.290 --> 22:43.190
sore ga boku no subete nanda sore ga boku wo karuku shiteru na

22:37.290 --> 22:43.190
That's my everything, and lifts the weight off my shoulders.

22:43.780 --> 22:48.260
mou doko he mo ikanaide

22:43.780 --> 22:48.260
Hey, don't go anywhere.

22:48.260 --> 22:53.720
yakusoku no basho wa itsumo hidamari no kaori wo sasete

22:48.260 --> 22:53.720
Our promised place always has the smell of sunshine.

22:53.720 --> 22:59.110
boku no ashimoto wo terashiteirunda

22:53.720 --> 22:59.110
It's casting a light at my feet.

22:59.110 --> 23:04.930
kimi no koto ga suki da yotte to ieru boku ga suki dakara

22:59.110 --> 23:04.930
I love myself being able to say "I love you!"

23:05.320 --> 23:10.610
mune no oku de sotto arigatou

23:05.320 --> 23:10.610
Softly in my heart I say, "Thank you."

23:16.630 --> 23:18.000
This is huge!

23:18.050 --> 23:19.460
Yes, it is.

23:19.820 --> 23:21.640
This is a nice room.

23:21.820 --> 23:22.710
I like it.

23:22.920 --> 23:24.750
Yes, it's a nice room.

23:26.040 --> 23:27.940
Sir, it's impossible!

23:27.980 --> 23:31.140
Please do something about this mountain of books!

23:31.560 --> 23:33.930
Nowaki! For now, you get out!

23:34.140 --> 23:34.940
Eh!?

23:35.540 --> 23:37.380
What kind of ki (tree) is this?

23:37.630 --> 23:39.420
Nowaki!!

23:40.420 --> 23:45.060
Raws: BDRIP (from nyaa.se)
Translation: aarinfantasy
